\label{thm:prime-local}
If $2\le\operatorname{wt}(X)\le p-2$, then
\[\boxed{s(f,X)=B_f(X)+N_f(X).}\]

Let $p$ be an odd prime and let $f$ be rotation symmetric on $p$ variables.  The local sensitivity at every necklace is given as follows:
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
\item at weights $0$ and $p$, by the first two formulas in the boundary-layer proposition;
\item at weights $1$ and $p-1$, by the two boxed boundary-layer formulas;
\item at weights $2,\ldots,p-2$, by Theorem~\ref{thm:prime-local} and Corollary~\ref{cor:explicit-prime}.
\end{enumerate}
Consequently, $s(f)$ is the maximum of these explicitly determined local quantities over the necklaces of length $p$.

Let $M_A$ be generated by a degree-$d$ monomial whose rotational stabilizer has order $h$.  Then
\[
\boxed{
s(M_A,1^n)=
\begin{cases}
n,&d/h\text{ is odd},\\
0,&d/h\text{ is even}.
\end{cases}}
\]
In particular, if $d/h$ is odd, then
\[
\boxed{s(M_A)=n.}
\]
